# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Orchestration System

> **Purpose:** Coordinate AI agents through specialized roles with proper context isolation.

---

## Quick Start

### Start Any Task
```
/do Add feature X
```

The Orchestrator runs in **fast-forward mode** by default:
- Shows an execution graph at start
- Auto-proceeds through steps
- Pauses ONLY at: **UX Discovery**, **Plan Approval**, **UAT**, **Merge Approval**
- Architect reviews always required (never skipped)

### Direct Role Invocation
```
/ux [feature description]    # Product/UX Lead - discovery & specs
/dev [task description]      # Dev - implementation & tests
/arch [PR or plan to review] # Architect - independent review
```

---

## Why Orchestration?

### The Problem

Without orchestration, AI collaboration breaks down:
- **Inconsistent handoffs** — Humans forget to invoke the right role
- **Self-review bias** — Same AI agent reviews its own work (useless)
- **Context leakage** — Architect sees Dev's reasoning, rubber-stamps
- **No accountability** — Unclear who did what in PR comments

### The Solution

Orchestration provides:
- **Automated workflow** — Right roles at right time
- **Context isolation** — Architect spawned separately, can't see Dev context
- **Clear accountability** — Each role posts verdict to PR
- **Human control** — Pauses at key decision points

---

## Core Concepts

### Roles

| Role | Focus | When Used |
|------|-------|-----------|
| **Orchestrator** | Coordinate workflow | Entry point for all work |
| **Product/UX Lead** | Requirements + interaction design | New features, UX changes |
| **Dev** | Implementation + tests | All coding work |
| **Architect** | Independent review (isolated) | Final quality gate before merge |

### Context Isolation (Critical)

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Pool 1: Discovery & Build          │
│  ├─ Product/UX Lead                 │
│  └─ Dev                             │
│     [Share context]                 │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘

┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Pool 2: Review (ISOLATED)          │
│  └─ Architect                       │
│     [Fresh context, no Dev memory]  │
│     [Reviews as stranger would]     │
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Why isolation matters:**
- Dev is biased toward their own code
- Architect catches what Dev missed
- Fresh eyes find hidden assumptions

**How it's enforced:**
- Architect spawned via Task tool (separate agent)
- Receives PR number only, not Dev's reasoning
- No access to planning discussions

### Workflow Tracks

Right-size review depth based on complexity:

| Track | Use For | Workflow |
|-------|---------|----------|
| **A: Full** | Features with UX | UX → Plan → Arch (plan) → Dev → UAT → Arch (code) → Human |
| **B: Standard** | Backend features | Plan → Arch (plan) → Dev → UAT → Arch (code) → Human |
| **C: Fast** | Simple bugs | Dev → Arch → Human |
| **D: Minimal** | Trivial fixes | Dev → Human |

**Note:** Architect review is ALWAYS required (even Track C/D). Never skip.

